# wip — spoken-form
# Started: 2026-11-12

#>plan_spoken_form
#:plan #!execution_truth
#:layer #!pragmatics

!["card"]{
 phase: #active
 gist: "A line is said in the names of its mark, slots and join, and every brace has a click whose timbre follows its label, both from the browser reader; what either should be is held as trials"
 touches: [~"packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/spoken.ts", ~"packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/pair-sound.ts", ~"packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/earcons.ts", ~"packages/spw-seed/src/reader.ts", ~"packages/spw-lsp/src/reader.ts", ~"packages/spw-seed/src/line/read.ts", ~"packages/spw-seed/src/canonical/geometry-inspect-position.ts"]
 entry: ~"./PLAN.md"
 next: "Someone listens: spw hear --line '<spw>' --out a.wav, and the same with --ear '^ear{ =voice[modal] }' to b.wav, and says which kinds, labels and closes they can tell apart in each; then no_audio_in_manifest."
}

^["edges"]{
 needs: [~"../pair-label-reading/wip.spw"]
 shares: [~"../interpretation-trials/wip.spw", ~"../line-kit/wip.spw", ~"../parse-columns/wip.spw"]
 feeds: [~"../host-receipts/wip.spw"]
}

^["roots"]{
 @plan: ~".agents/plans/spoken-form/PLAN.md"
 @trials: ~".agents/plans/interpretation-trials/interpretation-trials.spw"
 @slot_reader: ~"packages/spw-seed/src/line/read.ts"
 @names: ~"packages/spw-seed/src/line/names.ts"
 @reader_names: ~"packages/spw-seed/src/learn/readers.ts"
 @pair_labels: ~"packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/pair-labels.ts"
 @field_theory: ~"docs/theory/spw/em-fixity-association.spw"
 @field_dynamics: ~"docs/theory/spw/field-dynamics.spw"
 @release: ~"scripts/release/build-parser-release.ts"
}

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "A host can give a line an accessible name that keeps its mark, its slots and its join, and can let a listener hear which brace a close answers, from one browser bundle"
 ~#taste: "Say only the names of parts; keep every word in a table a host may replace; claim nothing about what anyone hears"
}

^["open"]{
 ?[heard]: "Nobody has heard either reader. What a screen reader says for the string, and whether the clicks help or tire, are a listener's to say."
 ?[underscore_said]: "kept_place is said kept place by default, which loses the joiner. Is the default a gap, the written word, or the host's choice only?"
 ?[surface_rows]: "A whole surface said as rows with a level and a position, for a tree widget, wants the parse columns. Is that the next slice, or a host's own work?"
 ?[shipped_samples]: "A story consumer's sound library names two sources, both CC0: Kenney's audio packs and the Versilian Community Sample Library at a pinned commit. Should a few samples ship here, or do synthesized clicks suffice?"
 ?[kind_apart]: "Five of the 21 bare clicks have the pitch of a click of another kind: a frame at depth d and a scene at depth d + 2. With whole-semitone gaps and a step of 2, three kinds cannot all stay apart unless the outer two sit more than 12 semitones apart. Keep kind on pitch and move the three notes, or carry kind on a texture (which overtones sound, how fast each dies away) and leave pitch to depth alone?"
 ?[depth_direction]: "A pair inside another is lower, so three closes in a row rise: 311, 349, 392 Hz. A larger body being lower is the other reading, and it would make an outer pair the low one. Which way does depth move pitch, or does depth leave pitch for something else?"
 ?[band_edge]: "The share of a click inside a band depends on the band. From 300 Hz, 6 of 21 bare clicks hold under half their energy in band and 0.8% of pairs here sit on one of them; from 400 Hz it is 13 of 21 and 46.2% of pairs, since a body at depth 0 is 392 Hz. Which low edge is a law held to: a fixed one, or the listener's own, written in the ear line?"
 ?[close_shape]: "A close is its open backward, so it holds none of its energy in its first 10 ms where the open holds 0.840. Keep the reversal, strike the close too and let it die away faster, or let an open ring until its close stops it? The last needs a host that holds a sound, and takes the place of a separate sound while a caret sits inside."
 ?[label_phrase]: "A label's timbre comes from a hash, so two labels one letter apart share nothing a listener could learn. A label could instead be a phrase of two or three notes from its letters, with the close playing the same phrase backward, as the stop phrase already does and as a mirrored close label is written. Which letters give which notes, and does the phrase take the place of the overtones or sit beside them?"
 ?[listener_words]: "A story consumer asks for user profiles: what a listener can use (lowest and highest pitch, one ear or two, speech rate). Here profile already means a syntax review profile and a lexing profile. Are these plain words in the ear line (%low, %high, =ears), or a named set, and under which word?"
 ?[speech_and_clicks]: "No reader here knows how long a host's voice takes to say a clause, so a law that a click never sounds over speech can only be about order. Is an ordered list of clauses and clicks enough, or does a host report the time each clause took?"
 ?[quest_flake]: "spw quest's whole-walk test took 5.3 s under a full CLI run and failed its 5 s limit once, then passed twice. Raise its limit, or make the walk lighter?"
}

^["commits"]{
 .[said_and_sounded](e664081f): "^seed[seed,lsp,release,trials,journal] — say a line in the names of its parts, give every brace a click whose timbre follows its label, and let a caret find the word inside a scope"
 .[slots_said](3f9e933e): "^seed[seed,journal,plans] — read what a mode, a scene and a concept hold, so a mark inside one is said by name"
 # Planned 2026-11-13 12:54, one change each, with the law that proves it. Every law reads rendered samples at 44,100 Hz with one transform size, 16,384. Today's number follows each law. sound_measures in the release plan lands first.
 # Until a listener picks, a change to the samples lands as a choice in the ear line whose default is today's samples, so ^ear{} renders the same and spw.pair-sound/1 keeps its id. The words given are first guesses. The words open, dwell, close, cues, wap, steps, pan and width are a story consumer's and are not taken here.
 ~[modal_voice]: "^seed[seed,release,sound] — a second voice for the brace sound, picked by =voice[modal] in the ear line, modelled on struck objects: kind as a texture, a label as a phrase, a struck and damped close, one level; without the word every click renders as before. Laws on rendered samples, each beside the first voice's number: no two kinds within 0.229 at any depth (first voice 0.000), every bare click over 0.5 of its energy in 300 to 3,000 Hz (first voice 0.027), every click within 1 dB of one level (first voice 7 dB), a close over half its energy in its first 10 ms (first voice none), a close's events its open's reversed. Clicks also carry span."
 ~[no_audio_in_manifest]: "![release] — hold that the parser release manifest lists no audio file. Law: no entry of a built manifest ends in .wav and none is made from rendered samples. Today: true, untested."
 ~[compare_two]: "^seed[sound] — let npm run sound:pairs render one source under two ear lines and print the measures of each side by side, so a tuning is chosen by comparing two. Law: both files hold the same clicks in the same order, and the two ear lines read back to the settings that made them."
 ~[span_echo]: "^seed[seed] — let an open carry a second, quieter copy of itself, later the more lines its pair spans, as %echo. Law: the lag of the strongest repeat never falls as span grows and stays under a stated ceiling, and a pair on one line renders the same samples as with no echo."
 ~[listener_words]: "^seed[seed] — read a listener's usable band and ears from the ear line, in the words picked at ?[listener_words]. Law: with a band written, every click holds at least half its energy inside it or the reading reports the click that cannot; a level is written in dB and a pitch step in semitones, and a written line reads back the same."
 ~[said_with_clicks]: "^seed[seed] — give one ordered list of a line's clauses and its clicks. Law: every click sits between two clauses and none inside a clause's span, over every line fixture and 1,500 generated lines."
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-11-12 23:20] observe — Prior words, counted before naming. A site consumer's caches hold a spoken twin (operator and slot names only, no connective words), a low-sight wonder cache of seven unanswered wonders, and the finding that its canvas names a node by the raw line. Here: the emit codec has an audio host for a script, the slot reader names four joins in a comment (a sequence, a list, a movement, a tight body), learn/readers.ts holds the operator names, and a trial card already asks whether a sound on a mark is a reading or a decoration (wonder_trial_modality). The field theory surfaces already call an open an accumulate port and a close a release port, and name permeability as a parameter that is a view field until a dialect implements it.
 >>[2026-11-12 23:42] surprise — The one red LSP test was not about labels. A caret inside @(topic) found the expression and stopped: findNodePathAtOffset walks a fixed list of child properties, and a postfix scope hangs on scope, which the list never gained when same-line postfix containers landed. capsule was missing too. The resolver's check for an @ before a scope also looked for two sibling expressions, the old shape.
 >>[2026-11-12 23:45] implement — The list gains scope and capsule; the resolver reads the operator from the expression that owns the scope. A new law walks every key of the tree and holds the lookup to reach a node at least as narrow as any node that starts at the caret, so the next property the parser gains fails a test instead of an editor.
 >>[2026-11-12 23:50] surprise — The slot reader split ^kept[thursday]{ .day[x] .chapter[y] } at its dots, as a tight body, and dropped the ground mark from each part. A tight dot now needs a word on both sides; a dot after a gap leads a word. Two fixtures hold it.
 >>[2026-11-12 23:58] decide — Spoken, not described or twin: the site consumer's word and the emit codec's. Slots are said by the reader column (definition) with the consumer's column beside it (body); joins by the slot reader's own words; a mark by its reader name, with #> anchor, #: lens and #! focus as the owner settled them. A host replaces any table, and may silence a join.
 >>[2026-11-13 00:05] decide — Parts set beside each other are said one after another, by reading what a reading leaves on its line again. That says a gap as beside without deciding wonder_trial_gap: the join table has a word for it and the default says nothing.
 >>[2026-11-13 00:10] decide — A body says where it ends when it held another pair, by its word or its label: end kept place, end thursday. A flat body does not. A pair label is said once at the open (labeled thursday) and once at the close, the same for a repeated and a mirrored close.
 >>[2026-11-13 00:20] implement — pairSound: kind is pitch (three notes of one chord), depth lowers it two semitones to a floor of six, a label picks the strength of five overtones in quarters from its letters, a close is its open's samples backward, an edge with no partner carries a tone at the square root of two above its pitch, and a stretch is bounded by three rising notes and the same notes falling. renderClick, renderPairSound and wavBytes are arithmetic only. The owner's notes are the design: a click with a timbre that changes with the label, and a start and stop phrase a listener learns.
 >>[2026-11-13 00:32] verify — 13 tests on the spoken form and 12 on the sound. Laws on the spoken form over every line fixture, 18 samples and 1,500 generated lines: nothing written is unsaid, nothing is said twice, and the written text of the clauses reads back to the source without its gaps. Laws on the sound, measured on rendered samples: a close is its open backward sample for sample, an open and its close hold the same overtones, each overtone comes out within 0.08 of what the label asks, a bare pair holds under 0.05 of any overtone, and the rough tone is over four times stronger on an edge with no partner. Five mutants: joins said alike, a close not reversed, a label ignored and no rough tone each fail one or two tests; a branch for a lone mark changed nothing and was removed, with a test for the line it was written for.
 >>[2026-11-13 00:40] verify — Census, .spw surfaces, worktrees and archives left out. Said line by line: here 163,611 lines, 59.0% with nothing unread, 1.0% of written characters unread; a story consumer 16,274 lines, 67.1% and 0.6%; the site consumer 217,485 lines, 63.2% and 0.7%. No line threw and none left a written character unsaid. Most of what is unread is a brace that opens on one line and closes on another, which a line-at-a-time reader cannot pair. Closes: of 74,524 pairs here 66.6% close on their own line, 7.9% close ten or more lines after they open, and 613 close forty or more lines after; 12 of those 613 carry a label. A story consumer has 71 such pairs and the site consumer 641, none labeled. Shapes: reading top-down, of subtrees of six or more nodes, 17.7% here, 20.5% and 26.3% in the consumers have a shape already met in the same surface.
 >>[2026-11-13 00:48] verify — Seed 1,152 pass, LSP 405 of 405, runtime 137, DOM 3, parser release 23, tsc clean. CLI 419 on two runs of three; on the first, spw quest's whole-walk test took 5.3 s against a 5 s limit under load, and it passes alone in 1.4 s.
 >>[2026-11-13 01:02] verify — The slot reader before and after the dot fix, over every line of three corpora: 4 of 172,022 lines read differently here, 198 of 17,267 in a story consumer and 13 of 225,487 in the site consumer. Each is a body where a dot led a word after a gap; before, the body was cut at that dot and the mark was lost.
 >>[2026-11-13 01:40] surprise — A review after the first commit found the coverage law passing for the wrong reason on three slots: a mode, a scene and a concept were each one clause over the whole bracket, said as written, so touches: [~"a", ~"b"] reached the string with its marks and nothing counted them. The law could not see it, because the clause covered every character.
 >>[2026-11-13 01:45] revise — Those slots are now read the way a body is: the slot's name, a join when it has one, and each part as a reading, with marks named. A tight dot is not a cut inside them, so work.how stays one word as written; how a dot is said stays with wonder_trial_dot. A test holds that no mark character reaches the string from inside a slot.
 >>[2026-11-13 01:50] verify — 14 tests on the spoken form. Recount over three corpora: 59.0%, 67.1% and 63.1% of lines with nothing unread; lines where an unquoted word, key or slot is still said with a mark or brace character in it: 413 of 163,748 here, 52 of 16,274 and 295 of 217,485, mostly tight forms the slot reader takes for one word and prose. The site consumer's 1,012 page expressions, from its generated manifest: all said with nothing unread, and none read differently by the slot reader before and after the dot fix. The journal said over 40 line fixtures; there are 34.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:54] note — The clock here reads 12:54. The last commit landed at 12:32 by the same clock, and the release plan's stream runs to 14:35, so its entries were stamped about two hours ahead. Entries from here use the machine's clock.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:54] observe — The owner asked the same day to think more about auditory design, physics and tuning, and for finer steps. A critique from the session was checked against rendered samples before any step was planned. Method: clicks rendered by renderClick at 44,100 Hz in node 23.1.0, a plain discrete transform of 16,384 points, energy summed between two frequencies; distance between two clicks is the distance between their power spectra, each scaled to length one. Nothing was heard, so each number says what samples hold and nothing about a listener.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:54] surprise — Kind and depth share one dial, and it shows in arithmetic before any ear. A frame at depth 0 and a scene at depth 2 are the same click: 523.25 Hz and 523.247 Hz, and no sample differs by more than 0.000037. The scene's note is four semitones above the frame's and a depth is two, so a frame at depth d matches a scene at depth d + 2 for d from 0 to 4: 5 of 210 pairings of the 21 bare clicks, the nearest 0.0000736 apart where a body and a frame at depth 0 are 1.376 apart. In tracked surfaces 41,373 frame pairs sit on those five pitches and 20 scene pairs do, so the confusion is met where a scene sits two deep. With whole-semitone gaps and a step of 2, three kinds cannot all be kept apart: two odd gaps add to an even one, so the outer two must sit more than 12 semitones apart.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:54] observe — What held of the critique, by number. A bare click low in pitch: a body at depth 6 is 196 Hz and holds 0.024 of its energy between 300 and 3,000 Hz; 6 of 21 bare clicks hold under half. A close: its power spectrum equals its open's to within rounding, its strongest sample sits at 42.6 ms where the open's sits at 2.4 ms, and it holds 0.000 of its energy in its first 10 ms where the open holds 0.840. Level: a labeled click is quieter than a bare one, because the overtones share one fixed peak; over the 9 written labels RMS runs 7.5 dB below the bare click, and over all 3,125 overtone settings 7.8 dB. Depth: three closes in a row rise, 311, 349, 392 Hz. One depth is 42.8 Hz at a body's pitch and a 45 ms click resolves about 22 Hz, so two neighbouring depths are about two widths apart.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:54] observe — What did not hold, or holds less than said. Shared timbres are possible (3,124 settings) and none is written: tracked surfaces hold 12 labeled pairs and 9 labels, and the 9 have 9 timbres; the nearest two, topography and geom, differ by one quarter on one overtone and sit 0.229 apart. All 12 are bodies at depth 0 spanning 93 to 376 lines, so a label has not yet met a depth. A low bare click is rare here: 577 of 74,722 pairs (0.8%) have a pitch under 300 Hz; with the edge at 400 Hz it is 34,489 (46.2%), because a body at depth 0 is 392 Hz, so the band edge decides the finding. A labeled click already carries overtones: at 196 Hz the 9 labels hold 0.236 to 0.727 in band. The count of pairs that close 40 or more lines later came to 580 of 74,722 over tracked surfaces against the journal's 613 of 74,524, a different set of files and not a correction. The render is one channel, so folding two ears to one changes nothing until a host pans. Whether Math.sin gives the same bits in two engines was not tested; two renders in one engine are the same, and the release manifest holds no audio.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:54] decide — Words, checked before use. Texture is the story consumer's word for a named sound and is kept for a kind's recipe of overtones and decay; material is already an axis of form geometry and is not taken. Phrase is already this module's word for notes in order and their reverse, so a label's notes are a phrase; motif is a namespace in a trial card and a consumer's word for six numbers. Profile already means a syntax review profile and a lexing profile, so a listener's settings stay plain words in the ear line until ?[listener_words] is answered. Open and close stay accumulate and release where the theory surfaces are meant.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:54] decide — The split. A step goes in tonight's release plan only if ^ear{} and PAIR_SOUND render the same samples before and after and no contract id moves; that admits a test file of measures, a paragraph of limits, and unknown ear words kept with their values. Every step that changes a sample, or waits on a choice, is a slice here. Order here: laws that need no ear first (no_audio_in_manifest, compare_two, kinds_apart, level_rms, bare_in_band, click_span), then the steps a listener or the owner picks between (close_struck, label_phrase, span_echo, listener_words, said_with_clicks). compare_two comes early because the later choices are made by comparing two renderings. A change to samples lands as a choice in the ear line with today's samples as the default, so each slice is additive and the defaults move once, with spw.pair-sound/2, after someone has listened.
 >>[2026-11-13 12:54] note — Not planned as commits: what a boundary lets through as a filter set by its kind waits on wonder_trial_permeability, which has no judgment; a sound held while a caret sits in a pair is the host's by the release plan and is one of the shapes at ?[close_shape]; shipped samples stay at ?[shipped_samples]. A root with ratios in place of three pitches in hertz is the same choice as ?[kind_apart] and is decided there.
 >>[2026-11-13 16:42] implement — The owner asked for an ambitious improvement. The 12:54 plan's six sample changes are built as one voice, modal-sound.ts, picked by =voice[modal]; without it every click renders the samples it rendered before, which a test holds for each kind and edge. Kind is a texture with textbook mode ratios (a free bar 1, 2.756, 5.404, 8.933; a string 1 to 6; a membrane 1, 1.594, 2.136, 2.296, 2.653, 2.918). A label is a phrase of up to three notes from its first, middle and last letters on a two-octave pentatonic ladder. A close is struck, damped 2.5 times harder, and plays its open's events in reverse order. Every click is scaled to one RMS, %level in the ear line. Clicks carry span.
 >>[2026-11-13 16:42] surprise — Textbook strengths did not meet the band law: with the first mode strongest, a bare bar at depth 6 (196 Hz) held 0.258 of its energy between 300 and 3,000 Hz. Strengths say where an object is struck, not what it is, so the bar is struck hard near its end (0.35, 1, 0.8, 0.4) and the string plucked near its end (0.4, 0.9, 0.9, 0.7, 0.55, 0.4); every bare click at depths 0 to 6 then holds at least 0.854, where the first voice's lowest held 0.027. The ratios are unchanged.
 >>[2026-11-13 16:42] surprise — A damped close puts its energy into a few milliseconds, so its peak sits up to 23.6 dB above its RMS. At a level of -20 dB one close had to be levelled to its peak; the default is -24 dB, and a level a click cannot reach is not reached, the click stopping at its peak, which a test states.
 >>[2026-11-13 16:42] verify — 9 tests on the modal voice, each law beside the first voice's number: nearest two kinds 0.588 apart over 21 bare clicks (first voice 0.000); in band at least 0.854 (first voice 0.027); level spread 0.00 dB (first voice 6.96); a close holds 0.661 of a labeled click's energy in 10 ms and loses half of it at 3.0 ms where the open does at 91.6 ms. Five mutants each fail a test: a phrase not reversed, no levelling, one texture for all kinds, an undamped close, a softly struck bar. Seed passes; release contract 25. npm run sound:pairs takes --ear, so one line renders under two tunings to two files. Nobody has heard either voice.
 >>[2026-11-13 16:42] decide — The questions stay open: the modal voice is one answer to kind_apart, close_shape and label_phrase, held as a choice a listener makes, and the first voice stays the default until someone listens.
 >>[2026-11-13 20:52] note — The listening step is one command now: spw hear --line '<spw>' --out a.wav, and again with --ear '^ear{ =voice[modal] }' to b.wav (36a853bb retired the script; npm run sound:pairs runs spw hear). That covers compare_two's rendering under two tunings; printing the two sides' measures side by side is what is left of it.
}

